### Serverless Order System API Tests
### Install "REST Client" extension in VSCode to use this file

# Variables - UPDATE THIS WITH YOUR API ENDPOINT
@baseUrl = https://YOUR-API-GATEWAY-ID.execute-api.us-east-1.amazonaws.com
@contentType = application/json

### Health Check
GET {{baseUrl}}/health
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

### Test 1: Create Low-Value Order (Standard Processing)
# Expected: SNS notification only, no SQS queue
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "order_id": "ORD-001",
  "customer_id": "CUST-123",
  "amount": 500
}

### Test 2: Create High-Value Order (Queued Processing)
# Expected: SNS notification + SQS message + ECS processing
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "order_id": "ORD-002",
  "customer_id": "CUST-456",
  "amount": 2500
}

### Test 3: Create Order at Threshold (Exactly $1000)
# Expected: SNS notification + SQS message
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "order_id": "ORD-003",
  "customer_id": "CUST-789",
  "amount": 1000
}

### Test 4: Order with Additional Fields
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "order_id": "ORD-004",
  "customer_id": "CUST-111",
  "amount": 3500,
  "product_id": "PROD-ABC",
  "quantity": 5,
  "notes": "Rush delivery requested"
}

### Test 5: Invalid Request - Missing Required Field
# Expected: 400 Bad Request
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "order_id": "ORD-005",
  "amount": 1500
}

### Test 6: Invalid Request - Invalid JSON
# Expected: 400 Bad Request
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "order_id": "ORD-006",
  "amount": "not a number"
}

### Test 7: Batch Test - Multiple Orders
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "order_id": "ORD-100",
  "customer_id": "CUST-BATCH-1",
  "amount": 750
}

